BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wheeler-centre-next-chapter-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Wheeler Centre: The Next Chapter 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Next Chapter is The Wheeler Centre's flagship writing progr
 am\, designed to elevate Australian stories that are underrepresented and 
 to nurture a new wave of writers to tell them. Each fellow receives a AUD 
 $15\,000 stipend and is paired with a handpicked mentor for a twelve-month
  period to progress a major writing project. Fellows also receive a reside
 ncy at Varuna\, The National Writers' House\; an end-of-year publishing in
 tensive at The Wheeler Centre\; and meaningful opportunities to connect wi
 th peers\, agents\, publishers\, and readers. One fellowship place is dedi
 cated specifically to a poet: The Malcolm Robertson Fellowship. 2027 judge
 s: Melissa Lucashenko\, Micaela Sahhar\, Cher Tan\, and Melanie Saward. EL
 IGIBILITY: Australian writers. No specific genre restrictions stated\; the
  program focuses on stories that are not currently being told and voices t
 hat are underrepresented. TIMELINE: submissions open 2 June 2026\; submiss
 ions close 31 July 2026 (5pm)\; 2027 Next Chapter Fellows announced 10 Nov
 ember 2026. Questions: thenextchapter@wheelercentre.com. Apply at https://
 www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chapter.\n\nOrganisation: The Wheeler Centr
 e\nLocation: Melbourne\, Australia\; includes residency at Varuna\, The Na
 tional Writers' House\, and an end-of-year publishing intensive at The Whe
 eler Centre.\nAward: AUD $15\,000 stipend per fellow. No application fee.\
 nDuration: 12 months.\n\nMore: https://www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chap
 ter?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chapter?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Melbourne\, Australia\; includes residency at Varuna\, The Nationa
 l Writers' House\, and an end-of-year publishing intensive at The Wheeler 
 Centre.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:adk-ems-berlin-stockholm-residency-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: AdK / EMS Berlin-Stockholm Bilateral Residency Program 20
 26-27
DESCRIPTION:A new bilateral residency collaboration between the Studio für
  Elektroakustische Musik at the Akademie der Künste in Berlin and Elektro
 nmusikstudion EMS in Stockholm. Four artists will be selected to develop a
 nd present new works in both cities\, with presentations at KONTAKTE 2027 
 in Berlin and at a corresponding event in Stockholm. The program supports 
 new artistic and technical initiatives at the intersection of sound\, musi
 c\, and technology in the field of time-based\, performative\, and digital
  arts. ELIGIBLE CATEGORIES: (1) new instrumental and live-electronic works
 \; (2) acousmatic music\, computer music\, radio art\, and other forms of 
 electroacoustic music and sound art\; (3) projects from artists of any dis
 cipline for whom sound is a central element\; (4) curatorial\, publishing\
 , and educational projects in sound-based art practice\, particularly thos
 e relating in content to the AdK Studio or EMS\; (5) independent research 
 in acoustics\, computer science\, or musicology -- specifically software d
 evelopment\, spatialization\, or network technologies. Open to individuals
  and groups. Project duration is flexible and arranged by agreement. SUPPO
 RT: travel and accommodation costs for Berlin and Stockholm covered\; pres
 entation fees paid for both venues. Selection is made by the director and 
 advisory board of the Studio für Elektroakustische Musik and the director
  of EMS\; decision is final with no legal entitlement to funding. Incomple
 te or late applications are not considered. This call supplements the Stud
 io's regular residency program (separate deadline June 30\, 2026 for July-
 December 2026 period). Apply exclusively via the online form at https://nc
 .adk.de/index.php/apps/forms/s/HD2nxbzqwgeMHWN6xHg9bQrA. Questions: estudi
 o@adk.de. Deadline: 31 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Studio für Elektroakus
 tische Musik\, Akademie der Künste (Berlin) and Elektronmusikstudion EMS 
 (Stockholm)\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany and Stockholm\, Sweden\; travel an
 d accommodation covered for stays in both cities.\nAward: Travel and accom
 modation costs for stays in Berlin and Stockholm covered\; fees paid for p
 resentation at KONTAKTE Festival 2027 (Berlin) and for presentation in Sto
 ckholm. Amount not publicly stated. No application fee.\nDuration: Flexibl
 e\, by agreement\; works to be presented at KONTAKTE 2027 in Berlin and at
  a Stockholm presentation.\n\nMore: https://nc.adk.de/index.php/apps/forms
 /s/HD2nxbzqwgeMHWN6xHg9bQrA?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://nc.adk.de/index.php/apps/forms/s/HD2nxbzqwgeMHWN6xHg9bQrA?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany and Stockholm\, Sweden\; travel and accommodation
  covered for stays in both cities.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kb-researcher-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Deadline: KB Researcher-in-Residence (RiR) 2027
DESCRIPTION:ELIGIBILITY: two Researcher-in-Residence positions in 2027. Ope
 n to early-career researchers of any discipline (data science\, social sci
 ence\, computer science\, humanities) who are currently working on a PhD o
 r within 5 years of their PhD end date. You must have\, or be able to secu
 re\, an affiliation with a Dutch university or research institute willing 
 to second you\; external PhD students may use the funding to obtain such a
  contract. Your project must make use of one or more of the KB digital col
 lections and you must be able to work with primarily Dutch data. You must 
 be available at 0.5 FTE over 6 months and able to spend two days a week on
 -site at the KB in The Hague. COLLECTIONS: over 130 million digitized page
 s of newspapers\, magazines\, radio bulletins and books from 1470 onward (
 via Delpher and DBNL)\, a born-digital web collection of more than 23\,000
  websites\, ground-truth and derived datasets on the KB Lab\, and metadata
  including Linked Data. APPLY: use the official proposal template and subm
 it a single PDF by 27 September 2026 to dh@kb.nl\, after reading the call'
 s terms and conditions\; questions to dh@kb.nl. TIMELINE: deadline 27 Sept
 ember 2026\; internal eligibility review followed by an external committee
  review\; outcome notified November 2026\; residencies start Q1 and Q3 202
 7. DISCIPLINES: digital humanities / data science / computational research
  with cultural-heritage collections. NOTE: the output is usually a dataset
  or tool prototype hosted on the KB Lab\; you agree to share results via b
 log posts on the KB Lab and to publish resulting tools or data under an op
 en license within 6 months of the residency. Proposals should align with t
 he KB Research Agenda or the Cultural AI Lab.\n\nOrganisation: KB\, Nation
 al Library of the Netherlands\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands (two days
  per week on-site at the KB premises)\nAward: Secondment at 0.5 FTE for 6 
 months based on your current salary\, up to EUR 5\,590 gross per month for
  a full-time-equivalent position\, plus travel expenses\, office facilitie
 s\, and support from a research software engineer\, research advisor\, and
  collection and data specialists. No application fee.\nDuration: 6 months 
 at 0.5 FTE (two days per week on-site)\; two positions in 2027\, starting 
 Q1 and Q3\n\nMore: https://lab.kb.nl/news/call-kb-researcher-residence-rir
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://lab.kb.nl/news/call-kb-researcher-residence-rir-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands (two days per week on-site at the KB premi
 ses)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ucross-general-residency-spring-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ucross General Residency (All Disciplines): Spring 2027
DESCRIPTION:Ucross offers fully funded artist residencies on a working catt
 le ranch in the foothills of Wyoming's Bighorn Mountains\, providing unint
 errupted time and space free from the pressures and distractions of daily 
 life. Founded in 1981 with its first residency period in 1983\, Ucross hos
 ts approximately 115 individuals per year. Residencies range from two to s
 ix weeks\; at any one time up to ten people are in residence\, typically f
 our writers\, four visual artists\, and two composers. Each artist receive
 s living accommodations\, meals\, and work space at no charge. Lunches and
  dinners are prepared Monday to Friday by a professional chef (lunches del
 ivered to studios\, group dinners at 6 p.m.)\, with ample provisions for b
 reakfasts and weekends\; towels\, linens\, and weekly housekeeping are pro
 vided\, and there is cell service and wireless internet throughout. Reside
 nts provide their own working materials and arrange their own travel to Sh
 eridan\, Wyoming. The program is open to visual artists\, writers\, compos
 ers\, choreographers\, interdisciplinary artists\, performance artists\, a
 nd collaborative teams\; applicants must exhibit professional standing in 
 their field\, and both established and emerging artists are encouraged to 
 apply. Applications are submitted by discipline category: dance\, music/so
 und\, performance\, film/video\, playwriting/screenwriting\, visual art\, 
 fiction\, nonfiction\, poetry\, or interdisciplinary. The work sample and 
 project proposal are the most significant features of the application and 
 should correspond to one another\; if your work is in a single discipline\
 , select the category that best fits your project\, and apply under interd
 isciplinary only if the project genuinely combines multiple disciplines. W
 ork-sample requirements by category: DANCE\, 2-3 video files (each up to 8
  minutes and 200 MB\, or up to 3 Vimeo links\, with a timestamp if longer 
 than 8 minutes)\; MUSIC/SOUND\, 3-5 audio files (each up to 8 minutes and 
 200 MB\, or up to 3 Vimeo links\; musical scores welcome)\; PERFORMANCE an
 d FILM/VIDEO\, 1-3 video files (each up to 5 minutes and under 200 MB\, or
  up to 3 Vimeo/YouTube links\, with a timestamp if longer than 5 minutes)\
 ; PLAYWRITING/SCREENWRITING\, one complete play double-spaced noting the 2
 0-page section to read\; VISUAL ART\, 10 images at 4x6 inches and 300 dpi 
 (JPG or TIF\, no PDFs) plus a data sheet listing title\, medium\, size\, a
 nd year\; FICTION and NONFICTION\, 20 pages of double-spaced writing\; POE
 TRY\, 6-10 poems (10 maximum) in one PDF\, each poem starting on a new pag
 e\, total not exceeding 15 pages\; INTERDISCIPLINARY\, samples representin
 g the genres you plan to work in\, combining any of the above. All written
  work samples must be in English. There is a USD 40 application fee. The o
 pen call for the Spring 2027 session is open May 1 to July 15\, 2026 (appl
 y by 11:59 p.m. MT on July 15). Dedicated Fellowships for Native American 
 Visual Artists and Writers and a separate Culinary Residency are also offe
 red.\n\nOrganisation: Ucross Foundation\nLocation: Sheridan\, Wyoming\, US
 A\nAward: No charge for the residency\; living accommodations\, meals\, an
 d work space provided. USD 40 application fee.\nDuration: Spring session (
 February through early June 2027)\; residencies range from two to six week
 s\n\nMore: https://www.ucrossfoundation.org/residency-program.html?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ucrossfoundation.org/residency-program.html?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sheridan\, Wyoming\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ucross-fellowship-native-american-writers-spring-2027@artificialnouveau
 .github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ucross Fellowship for Native American Writers: Spring 202
 7
DESCRIPTION:The Ucross Fellowship for Native American Writers is a dedicate
 d fellowship within Ucross Foundation's residency program\, offering fully
  funded time and space to write on a working cattle ranch in the foothills
  of Wyoming's Bighorn Mountains. The fellowship provides living accommodat
 ions\, meals\, and work space at no charge\, with no application fee. One 
 Fellowship winner is selected per session\; all applicants also have the o
 ption of being considered for a general Ucross residency. ELIGIBILITY: ope
 n to Native American writers who are practicing contemporary writers curre
 ntly producing work in one or more genres\, including but not limited to f
 iction\, nonfiction\, poetry\, drama\, screenwriting\, playwriting\, and h
 ybrid forms\; and who are enrolled members of a state-recognized or federa
 lly-recognized Tribe\, Pueblo\, Nation\, Native Community\, Political Enti
 ty\, or Alaskan Native Village. The work sample and project description ar
 e the most significant features of the application. Unless the work is gen
 uinely interdisciplinary (the genres interconnect)\, applicants are encour
 aged to apply in a single primary discipline and submit a work sample and 
 project description emphasizing that discipline. Work-sample requirements:
  FICTION\, 20 pages of double-spaced fiction (a novel excerpt\, a story\, 
 several stories\, or a combination)\; NONFICTION\, 20 pages of double-spac
 ed nonfiction\; POETRY\, 10 pages of poetry (may be single-spaced)\; PLAYW
 RITING\, one complete play (production documentation may be included if re
 levant)\, noting the 20 pages for reviewers to read\; SCREENWRITING\, one 
 complete screenplay (production documentation may be included if relevant)
 \, noting the 20 pages for reviewers to read. All writing samples should i
 nclude your full name. The open call for the Spring 2027 session closes Ju
 ly 15\, 2026 (apply by 11:59 p.m. MT). A separate Ucross Fellowship for Na
 tive American Visual Artists is also offered.\n\nOrganisation: Ucross Foun
 dation\nLocation: Sheridan\, Wyoming\, USA\nAward: Fully funded fellowship
  residency\; living accommodations\, meals\, and work space provided. No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: Spring session (February through early June 202
 7)\; residencies range from two to six weeks\n\nMore: https://www.ucrossfo
 undation.org/residency-program.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ucrossfoundation.org/residency-program.html?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sheridan\, Wyoming\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ucross-fellowship-native-american-visual-artists-spring-2027@artificial
 nouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ucross Fellowship for Native American Visual Artists: Spr
 ing 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Ucross Fellowship for Native American Visual Artists is a d
 edicated fellowship within Ucross Foundation's residency program\, offerin
 g fully funded time and space to make work on a working cattle ranch in th
 e foothills of Wyoming's Bighorn Mountains. The fellowship provides living
  accommodations\, meals\, and work space at no charge\, with no applicatio
 n fee. One Fellowship winner is selected per session\; all applicants also
  have the option of being considered for a general Ucross residency. ELIGI
 BILITY: open to Native American visual artists who are practicing contempo
 rary artists currently producing work in any visual medium\, including but
  not limited to painting\, drawing\, mixed media\, sculpture\, printmaking
 \, photography\, video\, animation\, performance art\, installation\, and 
 ceramics\; and who are enrolled members of a state-recognized or federally
 -recognized Tribe\, Pueblo\, Nation\, Native Community\, Political Entity\
 , or Alaskan Native Village. The work sample and project description are t
 he most significant features of the application. Unless the work is interd
 isciplinary\, applicants are encouraged to apply in a single primary disci
 pline and submit a work sample and project description emphasizing that di
 scipline. Work-sample requirements: VISUAL ARTWORK\, submit 10 images (JPE
 G format\, no PDFs) with file names including title and size\, plus a data
  sheet listing title\, medium\, size\, and year of completion for each ima
 ge\; FILM/VIDEO/ANIMATION/PERFORMANCE\, submit up to 3 video files (each u
 nder 8 minutes and smaller than 200 MB) or up to 3 Vimeo or YouTube links.
  The open call for the Spring 2027 session closes July 15\, 2026 (apply by
  11:59 p.m. MT). A separate Ucross Fellowship for Native American Writers 
 is also offered.\n\nOrganisation: Ucross Foundation\nLocation: Sheridan\, 
 Wyoming\, USA\nAward: Fully funded fellowship residency\; living accommoda
 tions\, meals\, and work space provided. No application fee.\nDuration: Sp
 ring session (February through early June 2027)\; residencies range from t
 wo to six weeks\n\nMore: https://www.ucrossfoundation.org/residency-progra
 m.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ucrossfoundation.org/residency-program.html?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sheridan\, Wyoming\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stiftung-kuenstlerdorf-schoeppingen-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stiftung Künstler*dorf Schöppingen: Residency Fellowshi
 p 2027 Open Call
DESCRIPTION:Stiftung Künstler*dorf Schöppingen offers residency fellowshi
 ps for professional visual artists\, authors and composers\; since 2023 ap
 plications from collectives are also accepted. The call is open to people 
 of all nationalities and ages\, and accommodation for partners\, family me
 mbers or assistance can be arranged upon agreement and availability (for p
 hysical\, cognitive or sensory disabilities\, contact the foundation to ex
 plain any barriers). Fellows reside and work at the Künstler*dorf for a p
 eriod of their choosing between two and six months\, using the premises an
 d infrastructure on-site. The stipend is EUR 1\,500 per month\, minus roug
 hly EUR 100-200 for rent and operating expenses\; for collectives it is EU
 R 1\,000 per person up to a maximum of EUR 3\,000 per month\, minus rent a
 nd operating costs. Travel\, insurance or material costs are covered only 
 in exceptional cases on request. The fellowship is not designed as a produ
 ction residency and there is no obligation to present results\, though exh
 ibition and presentation facilities are available and the voluntary co-org
 anization of events (lectures\, readings\, workshops or similar) is welcom
 ed. A willingness to participate in events and to engage in exchange with 
 other fellows is a prerequisite. Selection is made by expert juries on the
  quality of previous work\, the quality and plausibility of the project fo
 r Schöppingen\, and program contributions (interaction / community buildi
 ng). Applications for 2027 can be submitted from 27 June to 31 August 2026
  (midnight CET) via the online application portal.\n\nOrganisation: Stiftu
 ng Künstler*dorf Schöppingen\nLocation: Schöppingen\, Germany (residenc
 y requires living and working on-site)\nAward: Stipend of EUR 1\,500 per m
 onth\, minus roughly EUR 100-200 for rent and operating expenses. For coll
 ectives\, EUR 1\,000 per person up to a maximum of EUR 3\,000 per month\, 
 minus rent and operating costs. Travel\, insurance and material costs are 
 covered only in exceptional cases\, on request.\nDuration: Residency of tw
 o to six months during 2027\; period chosen by agreement and availability\
 n\nMore: https://stiftung-kuenstlerdorf.de/en/application_process?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stiftung-kuenstlerdorf.de/en/application_process?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Schöppingen\, Germany (residency requires living and working on-s
 ite)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:web-residencies-no-22-ignore-all-previous-instructions-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260808
SUMMARY:Deadline: Akademie Schloss Solitude: Web Residencies No. 22 - Ignor
 e All Previous Instructions
DESCRIPTION:Web Residencies No. 22\, 'Ignore All Previous Instructions\,' i
 s curated by !Mediengruppe Bitnik as part of Akademie Schloss Solitude's W
 eb Residencies program\, which since 2016 has supported young talents from
  the international digital scene as well as artists of all disciplines eng
 aging with web-based practices. For the tenth anniversary of the program\,
  this edition invites artists to create works that challenge extractive di
 gital platforms and AI systems\, exploring how to interrupt dominant techn
 ological logics\, from ad-tech surveillance to prompt injection vulnerabil
 ities\, and imagine alternative structures and communication methods. The 
 open call seeks proposals that hijack\, glitch\, and disrupt rather than c
 omply with existing systems\, drawing on strategies like Situationist deto
 urnement to map routes through and around the grids we are trapped within.
  Four to six proposals will be selected. BENEFITS: a four-week online resi
 dency\; a grant of EUR 1\,200\; a web space (microsite) on which the proje
 ct can be developed and published online\; support from a web/UX designer 
 and a programmer (in a supportive capacity only\, not to build an entire w
 ebsite)\; and participation in individual and group online events with the
  curators and Solitude fellows. Offline or hybrid formats (a reading sessi
 on\, panel\, exhibition\, or curated program) may follow. ELIGIBILITY: art
 ists of all disciplines may apply\, with no age limit\; submission is free
  of charge. The residency takes place exclusively online\, and selected fe
 llows agree to be available online during the four weeks. TIMELINE: the op
 en call runs from July 7 to August 7\, 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Akademie Sch
 loss Solitude\nLocation: Online (fully remote). Awarded by Akademie Schlos
 s Solitude\, Stuttgart\, Germany.\nAward: EUR 1\,200 grant for a four-week
  online residency\, plus a microsite to develop and publish the project\, 
 and support from a web/UX designer and a programmer in a supportive capaci
 ty.\nDuration: Four-week online residency.\n\nMore: https://application.ak
 ademie-solitude.de/fellowship-information/web-residencies?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://application.akademie-solitude.de/fellowship-information/web-res
 idencies?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (fully remote). Awarded by Akademie Schloss Solitude\, Stut
 tgart\, Germany.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Mondriaan Fund's Residency grant supports professional visu
 al artists\, curators\, and art observers who want to deepen their practic
 e through a residency in the Netherlands or abroad. It contributes to the 
 costs of a self-arranged residency that offers meaningful development for 
 the applicant's work. WHO CAN APPLY: visual artists\, curators\, and art o
 bservers who have been professionally active for at least one year and are
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. AMOUNT: th
 e grant amount varies depending on the residency's location and duration\;
  applicants must contribute at least 10% of the costs themselves\, through
  personal investment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\,
  or crowdfunding. APPLYING: submitted through the Mondriaan Fund's online 
 application portal\, which requires a pre-created account (allow several w
 orking days). DEADLINE: 27 August 2026\, 16:00 Dutch time (11:00 Caribbean
  time).\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund (Mondriaan Fonds)\nLocation: Nethe
 rlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part 
 of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherlands or abroad.\
 nAward: Grant amount varies depending on the location and duration of the 
 residency. Applicants must contribute at least 10% themselves (personal in
 vestment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\, or crowdfun
 ding).\nDuration: Varies by residency.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds
 .nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Ca
 ribbean part of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherland
 s or abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chornobyl40-open-call-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T080002Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260712
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260713
SUMMARY:Deadline: Chornobyl40: Open Call 2026 (Virtual Residency & Internat
 ional Exhibition)
DESCRIPTION:Chornobyl40 is a European artistic program\, funded by the Euro
 pean Union\, exploring the multiple legacies of the Chornobyl disaster not
  only as a past event but as an ongoing condition shaping the present and 
 future. The open call invites artists\, designers\, researchers\, collecti
 ves\, and interdisciplinary/hybrid practitioners to engage with Chornobyl 
 as a landscape\, a memory\, a political reality\, and a speculative horizo
 n. This is a call for interpretation\, friction\, and critical imagination
 \, not illustration. STRUCTURE (three phases): PHASE 1\, VIRTUAL RESIDENCY
 : 40 selected participants\, September-October 2026\, online\, weekly sess
 ions (Tuesdays 14:00-18:00 CET)\, 30 hours total with minimum 90% attendan
 ce\; a structured process from idea to concept to pre-production including
  talks on Chornobyl\, ecology\, and contaminated territories\, encounters 
 with artists and technologists\, a Concept Creation Hackathon\, an XR Conc
 ept Development Workshop (exploratory\, non-technical)\, a Mental Health &
  Eco-Anxiety Lab (4h)\, collective discussions\, peer feedback\, and tailo
 red mentoring. PHASE 2\, SELECTION & PRODUCTION: 20 projects selected (bas
 ed on a video presentation\, project documentation\, and a live pitch) rec
 eive production support. PHASE 3\, EXHIBITIONS: the 20 projects tour a Eur
 opean exhibition in 2027 (Madrid\, Berlin\, Toulouse\, Kyiv)\; artist pres
 ence optional but encouraged. WHAT'S OFFERED: for the 40 participants\, ac
 cess to a curated residency\, talks\, workshops\, mentoring\, and a Europe
 an network\; for the 20 selected projects\, a EUR 500 grant (fully digital
  works) or EUR 1\,000 grant (installations needing physical materials) plu
 s exhibition inclusion (travel\, accommodation\, and transport not covered
 ). WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, designers\, researchers\, collectives\, and in
 terdisciplinary/hybrid practices\; open internationally\, no age limit\, e
 merging and established profiles equally encouraged. PROJECT THEMES: ecolo
 gy and post-disaster environments\, memory and trauma\, geopolitical narra
 tives\, invisible forces (radiation\, data\, systems)\, technological imag
 inaries\, nuclear energy\, and misinformation and perception\; projects mu
 st relate to Chornobyl (directly or indirectly)\, be adaptable to multiple
  exhibition contexts\, and consider eco-responsibility\; new and adapted e
 xisting works both welcome. SELECTION CRITERIA (equally weighted): artisti
 c quality\, relevance to the manifesto\, eco-responsibility\, digital dime
 nsion\, and emotional and critical impact. TIMELINE: open call launched 19
  May 2026\; application deadline 12 July 2026\; 40 participants announced 
 end of July 2026. HOW TO APPLY: submit in English via the Google Form with
  a bio/CV link\, portfolio link\, and a project proposal (PDF\, 2 A4 pages
  maximum). Application is free. Questions: contact@gate22.net.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Chornobyl40 (gate22 / European Institute of Chornobyl consortium)\nL
 ocation: Online residency (weekly sessions Tuesdays 14:00-18:00 CET)\; Eur
 opean touring exhibition 2027 in Madrid\, Berlin\, Toulouse\, and Kyiv. Op
 en internationally.\nAward: Residency is free to attend. For the 20 projec
 ts selected for production: EUR 500 grant for fully digital works or EUR 1
 \,000 grant for installations requiring physical materials\, plus inclusio
 n in the international exhibition. Travel\, accommodation\, and transport 
 are not covered. No application fee.\nDuration: Phase 1 virtual residency 
 September-October 2026 (weekly Tuesday sessions\, 30 hours total\, minimum
  90% attendance). Phase 2 selection and production. Phase 3 European touri
 ng exhibition in 2027.\n\nMore: https://forms.gle/5btrxy7LwfY8QyFW6?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://forms.gle/5btrxy7LwfY8QyFW6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online residency (weekly sessions Tuesdays 14:00-18:00 CET)\; Euro
 pean touring exhibition 2027 in Madrid\, Berlin\, Toulouse\, and Kyiv. Ope
 n internationally.
END:VEVENT
